>>> grouped.boxplot(rot=45, fontsize=12, figsize=(8,10))  # doctest: +SKIP\n595 | \n596 |     The ``subplots=False`` option shows the boxplots in a single figure.\n597 | \n598 |     .. plot::\n599 |         :context: close-figs\n600 | \n601 |         >>> grouped.boxplot(subplots=False, rot=45, fontsize=12)  # doctest: +SKIP\n602 |     \"\"\"\n603 |     plot_backend = _get_plot_backend(backend)\n604 |     return plot_backend.boxplot_frame_groupby(\n605 |         grouped,\n606 |         subplots=subplots,\n607 |         column=column,\n608 |         fontsize=fontsize,\n609 |         rot=rot,\n610 |         grid=grid,\n611 |         ax=ax,\n612 |         figsize=figsize,\n613 |         layout=layout,\n614 |         sharex=sharex,\n615 |         sharey=sharey,\n616 |         **kwargs,\n617 |     )\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"group columns\", \"DataFrame.plot subplots group columns\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `pandas/core/groupby/grouper.py:Grouping.groups`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n695 | def groups(self) -> dict[Hashable, np.ndarray]:\n696 |         return self._index.groupby(Categorical.from_codes(self.codes, self.group_index))\n```\n\nFound class `asv_bench/benchmarks/groupby.py:Groups`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n114 | class Groups:\n115 | \n116 |     param_names = [\"key\"]\n117 |     params = [\"int64_small\", \"int64_large\", \"object_small\", \"object_large\"]\n118 | \n119 |     def setup_cache(self):\n120 |         size = 10**6\n121 |         data = {\n122 |             \"int64_small\": Series(np.random.randint(0, 100, size=size)),\n123 |             \"int64_large\": Series(np.random.randint(0, 10000, size=size)),\n124 |             \"object_small\": Series(\n125 |                 tm.makeStringIndex(100).take(np.random.randint(0, 100, size=size))\n126 |             ),\n127 |             \"object_large\": Series(\n128 |                 tm.makeStringIndex(10000).take(np.rando