ntinuous-multioutput'}\n 82 |         The type of the true target data, as output by\n 83 |         'utils.multiclass.type_of_target'.\n 84 | \n 85 |     y_true : array-like of shape (n_samples, n_outputs)\n 86 |         Ground truth (correct) target values.\n 87 | \n 88 |     y_pred : array-like of shape (n_samples, n_outputs)\n 89 |         Estimated target values.\n 90 | \n 91 |     multioutput : array-like of shape (n_outputs) or string in ['raw_values',\n 92 |         uniform_average', 'variance_weighted'] or None\n 93 |         Custom output weights if ``multioutput`` is array-like or\n 94 |         just the corresponding argument if ``multioutput`` is a\n 95 |         correct keyword.\n 96 |     \"\"\"\n 97 |     xp, _ = get_namespace(y_true, y_pred, multioutput, xp=xp)\n 98 | \n 99 |     check_consistent_length(y_true, y_pred)\n100 |     y_true = check_array(y_true, ensure_2d=False, dtype=dtype)\n101 |     y_pred = check_array(y_pred, ensure_2d=False, dtype=dtype)\n102 | \n103 |     if y_true.ndim == 1:\n104 |         y_true = xp.reshape(y_true, (-1, 1))\n105 | \n106 |     if y_pred.ndim == 1:\n107 |         y_pred = xp.reshape(y_pred, (-1, 1))\n108 | \n109 |     if y_true.shape[1] != y_pred.shape[1]:\n110 |         raise ValueError(\n111 |             \"y_true and y_pred have different number of output ({0}!={1})\".format(\n112 |                 y_true.shape[1], y_pred.shape[1]\n113 |             )\n114 |         )\n115 | \n116 |     n_outputs = y_true.shape[1]\n117 |     allowed_multioutput_str = (\"raw_values\", \"uniform_average\", \"variance_weighted\")\n118 |     if isinstance(multioutput, str):\n119 |         if multioutput not in allowed_multioutput_str:\n120 |             raise ValueError(\n121 |                 \"Allowed 'multioutput' string values are {}. \"\n122 |                 \"You provided multioutput={!r}\".format(\n123 |                     allowed_multioutput_str, multioutput\n124 |                 )\n125 |             )\n126 |     elif multioutput is not None:\n127 |         multioutput = check_array(multioutput, ensure_2d=False)\n128 |         if n_outputs == 1:\n129 |             raise ValueError(\"Custom weights are useful only in multi-output cases.\")\n130 |         elif n_outputs != multioutput.shape[0]:\n131 |             raise ValueError(\n132 |                 \"There must be equally many custom weights \"\n133 |                 f\"({multioutput.shape[0]}) as outputs ({n_outputs}).\"\n134 |             )\n135 |     y_type = \"continuous\" if n_outputs == 1 else \"continuous-multioutput\"\n136 | \n137 |     return y_type, y_true, y_pred, multioutput\n```\n"}, {"content": "It looks like the function `_check_reg_targets` is defined in `sklearn/metrics/_regression.py` and not in `test_regression.py`. Let's search `test_regression.py` for any calls to `_check_reg_targets` to identify relevant test cases.\n\n<function=search_code_snippets>\n<parameter=file_path_or_pattern>sklearn/metrics/tests/test_regression.py</parameter>\n<parameter=search_terms>[\"_check_reg_targets\"]</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "search_code_snippets", "content": "OBSERVATION:\nNo files found for file pattern 'sklearn/metrics/tests/test_regression.py'. Will search all files.\n...\n##Searching for term \"_check_reg_targets\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `sklearn/metrics/_regression.py:_check_reg_targets`.\nSource: Match found for entity name `_check_reg_targets`.\n```\n 58 | def _check_reg_targets(y_true, y_pred, multioutput, dtype=\"numeric\", xp=None):\n 59 |     \"\"\"Check that y_true and y_pred belong to the same regression task.\n 60 | \n 61 |     Parameters\n 62 |     ----------\n 63 |     y_true : array-like\n 64 | \n 65 |     y_pred : array-like\n 66 | \n 67 |     multioutput : array-like or string in ['raw_values', uniform_average',\n 68 |         'variance_weighted'] or None\n 69 |         None is ac