 Rounded values of the Series.\n2480 | \n2481 |         See Also\n2482 |         --------\n2483 |         numpy.around : Round values of an np.array.\n2484 |         DataFrame.round : Round values of a DataFrame.\n2485 | \n2486 |         Notes\n2487 |         -----\n2488 |         For values exactly halfway between rounded decimal values, pandas rounds\n2489 |         to the nearest even value (e.g. -0.5 and 0.5 round to 0.0, 1.5 and 2.5\n2490 |         round to 2.0, etc.).\n2491 | \n2492 |         Examples\n2493 |         --------\n2494 |         >>> s = pd.Series([-0.5, 0.1, 2.5, 1.3, 2.7])\n2495 |         >>> s.round()\n2496 |         0   -0.0\n2497 |         1    0.0\n2498 |         2    2.0\n2499 |         3    1.0\n2500 |         4    3.0\n2501 |         dtype: float64\n2502 |         \"\"\"\n2503 |         nv.validate_round(args, kwargs)\n2504 |         new_mgr = self._mgr.round(decimals=decimals)\n2505 |         return self._constructor_from_mgr(new_mgr, axes=new_mgr.axes).__finalize__(\n2506 |             self, method=\"round\"\n2507 |         )\n```\n\nFound function `pandas/core/internals/blocks.py:Block.round`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n1477 | def round(self, decimals: int) -> Self:\n1478 |         \"\"\"\n1479 |         Rounds the values.\n1480 |         If the block is not of an integer or float dtype, nothing happens.\n1481 |         This is consistent with DataFrame.round behavior.\n1482 |         (Note: Series.round would raise)\n1483 | \n1484 |         Parameters\n1485 |         ----------\n1486 |         decimals: int,\n1487 |             Number of decimal places to round to.\n1488 |             Caller is responsible for validating this\n1489 |         \"\"\"\n1490 |         if not self.is_numeric or self.is_bool:\n1491 |             return self.copy(deep=False)\n1492 |         # TODO: round only defined on BaseMaskedArray\n1493 |         # Series also does this, so would need to fix both places\n1494 |    